# The git-attest release the actions run, and the sha256 of each archive
# (decisions ADR-0037). fetch.sh downloads
# git-attest-<version>-<target>.tar.gz from that release, refuses it unless
# its digest is the one written here, and the actions fall back to verify.sh
# and sign.sh when it cannot. A commit therefore names the bytes its actions
# run: a swapped release asset is refused, not run.
#
# Written by the prepare-release workflow, committed in the release PR; never
# by hand. Between releases it names the last release, whose binary main's
# actions then run.
